###  https://purl.org/fairops/indiv#SimilarityRobustnessOfIndividualConsistency
indiv:SimilarityRobustnessOfIndividualConsistency rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                           core:DistanceBasedFairnessMetric ;
                                                  core:extends indiv:ConsistencyScore ;
                                                  core:isProposedBy <https://purl.org/fairops/papers#2025_WALLER> ;
                                                  core:isSuitableFor core:Prediction ,
                                                                     core:Recommendation ;
                                                  core:measures indiv:FairnessThroughAwareness ;
                                                  core:refersTo core:Classification ;
                                                  core:scientificArtifactDescription """SRIC quantifies the proportion of individuals for which the individual
consistency falls below or rises above a threshold $\\delta$ when comparing
two different notions of similarity $\\sigma_i$ and $\\sigma_j$.
\\begin{equation}
\\text{SRIC}^{\\delta}_{\\{\\sigma_i,\\sigma_j\\},k}
=
\\frac{1}{|E|}
\\left|
\\left\\{
x \\in E :
\\big(c^{\\sigma_i,k}(x) \\ge \\delta \\wedge c^{\\sigma_j,k}(x) < \\delta \\big)
\\ \\vee\\
\\big(c^{\\sigma_i,k}(x) < \\delta \\wedge c^{\\sigma_j,k}(x) \\ge \\delta \\big)
\\right\\}
\\right|
\\end{equation}
SRIC is defined with respect to a threshold $\\delta$, which specifies the
required proportion of similar individuals receiving equivalent treatment.""" .


